Appendix A 1A post-stir formula വലിയ exact old snapshot-ിൽ പരിശോധിക്കുന്ന clean Stage 1 fixture. six old bowls എല്ലാം M, stir=1. `savedStirSum=SAVE(6M+149)=149`, അതിനാൽ order rank 149. position-order pending values full formula വഴി കണക്കാക്കുന്നു; order materialization വേറെയുള്ള rank-to-order probe-ന്റെ ഉത്തരവാദിത്തമാണ്.

Hamlet, M സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Juliet, savedStirSum സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Romeo, order rank സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Othello, pre-square s സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Macbeth, pending value സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Lady Macbeth, position സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Ophelia, doubling count സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Prospero, flow-വും assignment-വും സഹായിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.

Act I: M നിർമ്മിക്കുന്നു.

Scene I: one, count 127.
[Enter Prospero and Hamlet]
Prospero:
 You are a hero.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Ophelia]
Prospero:
 You are as good as the difference between a big big big big big big big hero and a hero.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Hamlet and Ophelia]

Scene II: doubling loop.
Hamlet:
 Are you better than nothing?
Ophelia:
 If not, let us proceed to scene III.
Hamlet:
 You are as good as the difference between yourself and a hero.
Ophelia:
 You are as good as the product of yourself and a big hero.
 Let us return to scene II.

Scene III: M=2 power 127 minus 1.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Hamlet]
Prospero:
 You are as good as the difference between yourself and a hero.

Act II: 1A saved sum-വും order rank-ും.

Scene I: savedStirSum = SAVE(6M+149).
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Juliet]
Prospero:
 You are as good as the product of the sum of a big big hero and a big hero and Hamlet.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and the sum of the sum of a big big big big big big big hero and a big big hero and the sum of a big big hero and a hero.
 You are as good as the difference between yourself and a hero.
 You are as good as the remainder of the quotient between yourself and Hamlet.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and a hero.
 Open your heart.
[Exeunt]

Scene II: rank = 1 + regularMod(saved-1,720).
[Enter Prospero and Romeo]
Prospero:
 You are as good as the difference between Juliet and a hero.
 You are as good as the remainder of the quotient between yourself and the sum of the sum of a big big big big big big big big big hero and a big big big big big big big hero and the sum of a big big big big big big hero and a big big big big hero.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and a hero.
 Open your heart.
[Exeunt]

Act III: six positions-ന്റെ full post-stir arithmetic.

Scene I: position 1.
[Enter Prospero and Lady Macbeth]
Prospero: You are a hero.
 Let us proceed to scene VII.

Scene II: position 2.
[Enter Prospero and Lady Macbeth]
Prospero: You are a big hero.
 Let us proceed to scene VII.

Scene III: position 3.
[Enter Prospero and Lady Macbeth]
Prospero: You are as good as the sum of a big hero and a hero.
 Let us proceed to scene VII.

Scene IV: position 4.
[Enter Prospero and Lady Macbeth]
Prospero: You are a big big hero.
 Let us proceed to scene VII.

Scene V: position 5.
[Enter Prospero and Lady Macbeth]
Prospero: You are as good as the sum of a big big hero and a hero.
 Let us proceed to scene VII.

Scene VI: position 6.
[Enter Prospero and Lady Macbeth]
Prospero: You are as good as the sum of a big big hero and a big hero.

Scene VII: s = M + 3M + 5M + saved + stir + position squared.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Othello]
Prospero:
 You are as good as Hamlet.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and the product of the sum of a big hero and a hero and Hamlet.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and the product of the sum of a big big hero and a hero and Hamlet.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and Juliet.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and a hero.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and the product of Lady Macbeth and Lady Macbeth.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Macbeth]
Prospero:
 You are as good as the product of Othello and Othello.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and the product of the sum of the sum of a big big hero and a big hero and a hero and the product of Hamlet and Hamlet.
 You are as good as the difference between yourself and a hero.
 You are as good as the remainder of the quotient between yourself and Hamlet.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and a hero.
 Open your heart.

Scene VIII: അടുത്ത position തിരഞ്ഞെടുക്കുന്നു.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Lady Macbeth]
Lady Macbeth:
 Am I as good as a hero?
Prospero:
 If so, let us proceed to scene II.
